/T (Our approach to Torah at Yeshivat Moreshet Yerushalayim is rooted in the rich traditions of Sephardic heritage. We teach Gemara, Tur and Bet Yosef through the Sephardic approach. In Halakha classes, there is a strong emphasis on community minhagim. Our students are encouraged to hazzen, sharpening their hazzanut skills and building their confidence. This year, several students learned how to read the Megillah for Purim. Their hard work is a gift to our community that was not only enjoyed this year, but will continue to be so for many years to come.)
/E (Our approach to Torah at Yeshivat Moreshet Yerushalayim is rooted in the rich traditions of Sephardic heritage. We teach Gemara, Tur and Bet Yosef through the Sephardic approach. In Halakha classes, there is a strong emphasis on community minhagim. Our students are encouraged to hazzen, sharpening their hazzanut skills and building their confidence. This year, several students learned how to read the Megillah for Purim. Their hard work is a gift to our community that was not only enjoyed this year, but will continue to be so for many years to come.)
